      "description": "Watch Amed vs Besiktas highlights and goals from Süper Lig on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 20, 2026. The Süper Lig clash between Amed SF and Beşiktaş on September 20, 2026, delivered a high-stakes encounter filled with tactical shifts and individual brilliance. Both sides entered the pitch looking to assert their dominance in a match that kept the fans on the edge of their seats until the final whistle. Early Dominance from the Hosts Amed SF started the match with blistering intent, pinning their opponents back from the opening whistle. The early pressure paid dividends in the 13th minute when Gift Orban found the back of the net to break the deadlock. The momentum stayed firmly with the home side, and just nine minutes later, Gift Orban turned provider, delivering a precise assist for Dia Saba to double the lead in the 22nd minute. Beşiktaş struggled to find their rhythm during a feisty first half characterized by several bookings. The referee was kept busy as Mohamed Khalil , Ermal Krasniqi , and Ilhan Fakili all entered the book before the interval, reflecting the physical nature of the contest as the visitors tried to claw their way back into the game. A Resilient Comeback Attempt At the start of the second half, Beşiktaş made a triple substitution, introducing Vaclav Cerny , Fabio Miretti , and Emirhan Topcu to spark a revival. The tactical shift worked as Dusan Vlahovic pulled a goal back in the 55th minute, giving the visitors a lifeline. However, any hopes of a quick equalizer were dashed just four minutes later when Furkan Soyalp restored the two-goal cushion for Amed SF , making it 3-1. Late Drama and Nerves of Steel The match took a dramatic turn in the closing stages when Amadou Cisse , who had come on as a substitute, received two yellow cards in quick succession, resulting in a red card in the 84th minute. Down to ten men, Amed SF faced an onslaught. In the 8th minute of stoppage time, Orkun Kokcu converted a penalty for Beşiktaş to set up a grandstand finish. Despite the intense pressure and further yellow cards for Mehmet Yesil and Emirhan Topcu , Amed SF held firm through twelve minutes of added time to secure a thrilling victory."
